(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-framing-decision :authorize-foundation-pour :proceed-with-structural-work :override-safety-officer-judgment :override-foreman-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage" "2799009331-cloud-itonami-isco-9331-hand-and-pedal-vehicle-drivers-coverage" "2799009332-cloud-itonami-isco-9332-animal-drawn-vehicle-drivers-coverage" "2799008350-cloud-itonami-isco-8350-ships-deck-crews-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the framing work" "proceed with the foundation work" "finalize the framing decision" "authorize the foundation pour" "finalize the foundation pour decision" "override the foreman's safety judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override the site safety officer's judgment" "override foreman safety judgment" "override site safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007111), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :construction/house-building-site-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :builder-verified :site-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7111"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007111: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7111 House Builders job-site scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7111\n-- House Builders** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7111\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"7111\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"House Builders\" -- confirming\nthe premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity`\nwas `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics :identity\n:audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed\nat `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111` (`gh api` 404 confirmed\nbefore scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote\nthe `7111` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nHouse Builders perform structural construction work on active job\nsites -- real physical-safety stakes (falls, structural collapse,\nequipment injury). The controlling constraint for this vertical is\nthat the closed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly\nfinalizes a structural-work-execution decision (e.g. deciding to\nproceed with a specific framing or foundation step), or overrides a\nsite safety officer's or foreman's judgment -- those decisions must\nalways be a hard permanent block or an always-escalate op, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to JOB-SITE\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never performs\nconstruction work itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set) -- cloned\nand read in full in this session. The physical-safety-domain shape\n(closed allowlist + always-escalate safety flag + content-based\nscope-exclusion with a self-trip regression test) was mirrored closely\nfrom the most recent sibling in the same wave,\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9311`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9311)\n(Mining and Quarrying Labourers) -- also cloned and read in full.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111` as an OSS job-site\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for house builders, following\nthe SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **House Builder Advisor\n⊣ HouseBuilderGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **job-site scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct construction-work-execution authority** -- it must\nNEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose\nexercising a structural-work-execution decision (e.g. a specific\nframing or foundation step), or any override of a site safety\nofficer's or foreman's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- task/materials-usage/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a structural-integrity/site-hazard/\n  crew-fatigue concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- building-materials procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nstructural-work-execution decision or a site-safety-officer/foreman-\njudgment override. These are **structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op\nsuch as `:finalize-framing-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names five\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`housebuilder.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-framing-decision`, `:authorize-foundation-pour`,\n`:proceed-with-structural-work`, `:override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-foreman-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is verified by\ndedicated unit tests\n(`housebuilder.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-framing-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-foundation-pour`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-foreman-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Builder unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered builder record (`:no-builder`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the builder is.\n2. **Site unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered job site (`:no-site`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a builder/site\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with framing\n   or foundation work, or overriding a site safety officer's or\n   foreman's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks structural-work-execution/safety-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a structural-integrity/\n  site-hazard/crew-fatigue observation -- it never resolves the\n  concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about site safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  building-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  structural-work-execution or safety-officer-override attempt, which\n  is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft escalate vs.\n  structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"framing\", \"foundation\", \"safety\", \"foreman\") can accidentally\nmatch inside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a\nlegitimate proposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this\nis exactly the risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a job-site\ncoordination actor working adjacent to framing/foundation work\nnecessarily discusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job)\ncould trigger if phrased carelessly.\n`housebuilder.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the framing\nwork\", \"authorize the foundation pour\", \"override the foreman's\nsafety judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example phrasing),\nnever bare nouns, and\n`housebuilder.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for builder ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for framing\ntask ...\", \"... routed for site safety officer review\") WITHOUT\ncontaining any of the full finalization-action phrases, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-\nphrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on first run in this\nsession -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never\ntripped during development. `housebuilder.actor-test/holds-a-scope-\nexcluded-op-even-at-high-confidence` additionally exercises the same\ninvariant through the full graph run, confirming a scope-excluded\nproposal never reaches `commit-record!` regardless of disposition\npath.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7111\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7111`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 21 tests, 45 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-framing-decision` or\n  `:approve-foundation-pour` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means\n  the *capability* to finalize a structural-work-execution decision\n  exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For\n  a decision this severe (falls, structural collapse, equipment\n  injury), the capability itself must not exist. The only op related\n  to site-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces\n  the need for human/site-safety-officer attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers a structural-work decision for later\n  automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold building-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the structural-work-execution/\n  safety-officer-override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"framing\"\n  \"foundation\" \"safety\" \"foreman\"]`): rejected outright per the\n  fleet-known self-trip bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own\n  worked example for this exact task), and per the explicit instruction\n  to phrase scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS,\n  never bare nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  framing/foundation/safety-officer concepts to do its\n  scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking\n  the actor's own legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly\n  against rationale text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `builder` and `site` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered builder AND independently-registered site)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"builder/site record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- task/materials-usage/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered builder AND\n   site (`:no-builder`/`:no-site`). Not a structural-work-execution or\n   safety-officer decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a structural-work-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific framing or foundation step -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a structural-integrity/site-\n   hazard/crew-fatigue concern to a human/site safety officer; ALWAYS\n   escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the site safety\n   officer or foreman reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- building-materials procurement\n   proposal only (item, cost). Not a structural-work-execution or\n   authorization decision of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics\n   action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000\n   always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na structural-work-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with a specific\nframing or foundation step) or a site-safety-officer/foreman-judgment\noverride -- these categories are structurally absent, not gated,\nconfirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`housebuilder.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`housebuilder.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`housebuilder.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-framing-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-foundation-pour`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-foreman-judgment`), and (c) a\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op` field\n(`housebuilder.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with framing work or override a foreman's\nsafety judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`housebuilder.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-foreman`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-17"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 21, :assertions 45, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "House Building Site Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :builder-verification :site-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7111"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)), (:test/simulator :housebuilder.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7111 — House Builders Job-Site Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7111)))
